From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm: a solo prompt step runs between request starts

TF_GLM_REQUEST_STARTS=1 cuts a prompt pass at each message start, and a request with any cut took no solo step
(TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO=4096): prompt_solo.at, prompt_solo.allowed and cuda_prompt_cuts.stepRows each refused a solo-sized
step when the request had a cut. A chat prompt has a message start after row 0, so every chat request under request
starts ran in 2,048-row steps. On three GB10s at TP=3 a cold first token with request starts read 4.1%, 6.5% and 7.2%
slower than without at 8k, 32k and 120k, within 1% of the CHUNK_SOLO-only arm, and a ~113k cold prime 7.3% slower.

The cold plan is unchanged: a pass cuts every 2,048 rows from 0 and at each start (nextCut, coldCut), and a kept
state resumes only at a cold cut (resumes, below). A solo step is two such chunks run as one pass, so with no start
inside it, it begins and ends on cold cuts, and its middle grid point is a point the plan has no start at. cutInside
names the one case that is not allowed: a start after the step's first row and before its end (a start at its end is
the next step's first row). prompt_solo.at (rank 0's choice), prompt_solo.allowed (every rank's check of the step) and
stepRows (the part's length) all use it, so the ranks agree on every step; takesTwo still refuses a step whose middle
grid point holds a keep mark. A request with no cut is unchanged: cutInside is false for an empty list. Pairing
(TF_GLM_PROMPT_PAIR) still refuses a request with cuts.

Replies are CHUNK_SOLO's: upstream's contract is the same tokens as 2,048-row passes. Receipts: the host tests of
cuda_prompt_cuts (stepRows, cutInside, the leader-rows walk over the cut lists). The GPU receipts (cold first token and
replies with request starts on and solo on, against solo alone and request starts alone) are not in this header.

New here, not a re-seat: written at v1.2.9 on top of this repo's stack (patches/engine, pr1411, cache-salt and
learn-starts). Its docs hunk sits on learn-starts' text of the request starts paragraph, which now says that a pass
with starts takes a solo pass only where no start is inside it.

---

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_prompt_cuts.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_prompt_cuts.zig
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_prompt_cuts.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_prompt_cuts.zig
@@ -49,12 +49,19 @@
     try list.appendSlice(gpa, cuts);
 }
 
-/// A prompt step's rows from `start` with `part_len` ids: to the next cut, or a solo pass's when `part_len` holds more.
+/// Whether a request start lies inside the step of `rows` from `start`: past its first row, before its end.
+pub fn cutInside(cuts: []const u32, start: usize, rows: usize) bool {
+    for (cuts) |c| if (c > start and c < start + rows) return true;
+    return false;
+}
+
+/// A prompt step's rows from `start` with `part_len` ids: to the next cut, or a solo pass's when no start is inside it.
 pub fn stepRows(len: usize, cuts: []const u32, start: usize, part_len: usize) !usize {
     if (start >= len or !coldCut(len, cuts, start)) return error.BadChunk;
     if (part_len <= prefill_rows + 1) return nextCut(len, cuts, start) - start;
-    if (cuts.len > 0) return error.BadChunk; // a solo pass would step over a request start
-    return @min(len - start, state.solo_rows);
+    const rows = @min(len - start, state.solo_rows);
+    if (cutInside(cuts, start, rows)) return error.BadChunk; // a solo pass would step over a request start
+    return rows;
 }
 
